"""Practical examples from the European Commission's draft guidelines on the
classification of high-risk AI systems (19 May 2026), as published on the
EU AI Act Service Desk (ai-act-service-desk.ec.europa.eu). Descriptions are
short paraphrases; the verdict is the Commission's.

verdict: "high" = should be classified high-risk, "not" = should not.
reason:  "in" (in the use case), "out" (outside the use case / not covered),
         "6.3a".."6.3d" (Article 6(3) filter condition).
split:   "dev" areas were used while building the skill; "holdout" areas were
         frozen and only used once for the final blind test.
"""

